{"annotations": [], "blocks": [{"bbox": [42.5196, 29.611933999999906, 367.6936026000012, 35.33202199999994], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 0, "source": "docling", "text": "10"}, {"bbox": [42.5196, 58.27306599999997, 320.81132131000004, 65.31297800000004], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "caption", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 1, "source": "docling", "text": "Table 3 TEAEs of grade ≥ 3 occurring in at least 2 patients in any treatment group."}, {"bbox": [42.5196, 298.017066, 218.66525135999998, 304.61697799999996], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 2, "source": "docling", "text": "Abbreviation: TEAE, treatment-emergent adverse event."}, {"bbox": [42.51959999999997, 321.972, 288.081, 387.9453], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 3, "source": "docling", "text": "inhibition,  a  phenomenon  that  has  been  reported  in  studies  of solid  tumors  and  can  eventually  lead  to  drug  resistance. 27,28 Better understanding of the role PI3K signaling plays in myelofibrosis could inform additional targets within this pathway that could  be  inhibited  simultaneously  to  counteract  an  adaptative response."}, {"bbox": [42.5196, 391.5336, 288.11340000000007, 562.0484999999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 4, "source": "docling", "text": "In conclusion, findings from  the interim analysis of the LIMBER-304  study  suggested  adding  parsaclisib  to  stable-dose ruxolitinib was unlikely to provide clinically meaningful benefits in  heavily  pretreated  patients  with  myelofibrosis  and  suboptimal or declining response to ruxolitinib, resulting in study termination. The overall incidence of TEAEs was similar between the 2 treatment groups, but there was a greater incidence of serious, severe,  and  fatal  TEAEs,  as  well  as  infection  and  GI  disorders with  the  parsaclisib/ruxolitinib  combination.  Given  the  overall findings, close monitoring for infections and toxicities and reassessment of benefit-risk for patients on combination therapy is warranted.  Further  investigations  may  clarify  if  PI3K  inhibitors could  have  a  role  in  selected  patient  subsets,  or  in  alternative combinations, as potential therapeutic strategies in myeloproliferative neoplasms."}, {"bbox": [42.5196, 583.457934, 169.23291749999999, 597.0980219999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 5, "source": "docling", "text": "Acknowledgments"}, {"bbox": [42.51959999999997, 605.606, 288.12059999999997, 671.6353999999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 6, "source": "docling", "text": "The authors thank the patients, investigators, and site personnel who participated in this study. This study was funded by Incyte Corporation  (Wilmington,  DE).  Medical  writing  assistance  was provided by Steven Moore, PhD, of Envision Ignite, an Envision Medical  Communications  Agency,  a  part  of  Envision  Pharma Group, and funded by Incyte Corporation."}, {"bbox": [42.5196, 693.0453339999999, 186.98208200999997, 706.685422], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 7, "source": "docling", "text": "Author contributions"}, {"bbox": [42.51959999999997, 715.1936999999999, 288.08910000000003, 734.7354], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 8, "source": "docling", "text": "Jean-Jacques  Kiladjian  (Investigation,  Validation,  Visualization, Writing-review & editing), Uma Borate (Investigation, Writingreview & editing), Elisabetta Abruzzese (Investigation, Writing-review  &  editing),  Valerio  De  Stefano  (Investigation, Writing-review & editing), Tiejun Gong (Investigation, Writingreview  &  editing),  Massimo  Breccia  (Investigation,  Writing-review  &  editing),  Francesca  Palandri  (Investigation,  Writingreview  &  editing),  Fabrizio  Pane  (Investigation,  Writing-review &  editing),  Andrea  Patriarca  (Investigation,  Writing-review  & editing),  Hakon  Reikvam  (Investigation,  Writing-review  &  editing), Lindsay Rein (Investigation, Writing-review & editing), Abdulraheem Yacoub (Conceptualization, Investigation, Visualization, Writingreview  &  editing),  Feng  Zhou  (Data  curation,  Formal  analysis, Software, Visualization, Writing-original draft, Writing-review & editing), Michael Stouffs (Conceptualization, Data curation, Funding acquisition, Methodology, Supervision, Visualization, Writing-original  draft,  Writing-review  &  editing),  Albert  Assad (Conceptualization, Data curation, Funding acquisition, Methodology,  Supervision,  Visualization,  Writing-original  draft, Writing-review & editing), and Alessandro Maria Vannucchi (Investigation, Writing-review & editing)"}, {"bbox": [303.307, 565.882934, 471.81323712999995, 579.523022], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 9, "source": "docling", "text": "Supplementary material"}, {"bbox": [303.307, 588.031, 534.1327, 595.951], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 10, "source": "docling", "text": "Supplementary material is available at The Oncologist online."}, {"bbox": [303.307, 617.359934, 359.40186190000003, 631.000022], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 11, "source": "docling", "text": "Funding"}, {"bbox": [303.307, 639.5649999999999, 548.8792000000001, 659.3901999999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 12, "source": "docling", "text": "This  study  was  sponsored  by  Incyte  Corporation,  Wilmington, DE, USA."}, {"bbox": [303.307, 680.799734, 439.56527908000004, 694.4398219999999], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "heading", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 13, "source": "docling", "text": "Conflicts of interest"}, {"bbox": [303.307, 702.948, 548.8738, 734.7351], "bold": null, "confidence": 1.0, "font_size": null, "kind": "paragraph", "ocr_engine": null, "page": 10, "seq": 14, "source": "docling", "text": "J.-J.K.: Consultancy and advisory boards for AbbVie,  AOP Health, BMS, GSK, Incyte Corporation, and Novartis. U.B.: Consultant  for  AbbVie, Astellas,  Daiichi  Sankyo,  Genentech,"}], "checksum": "b4d81834dac0d2181403874c3a59496862b880293b625d290b8b2dab34226f53", "content_present": true, "doc_id": "d-730339a6f12064a3", "docling_version": "2.118.0", "engine_version": "2.118.0", "errors": [], "images": [], "page_index": 9, "page_sizes": {"10": [595.2760009765625, 782.3619995117188]}, "route": "docling", "schema_version": "v0.1.0", "source_hash": "730339a6f12064a3ce1677bdb0cc37f7165e2a98364d9c7cb4512c3130599815", "status": "ok", "tables": [{"bbox": [41.14227898223325, 70.02306134658193, 547.688629373908, 292.7534076711401], "body_bottom": 289.0152999999999, "caption": "Table 3 TEAEs of grade ≥ 3 occurring in at least 2 patients in any treatment group.", "cell_bboxes": [[[42.5196, 108.5788, 99.1296, 116.49879999999996], null, null, null], [[51.5331, 120.08709999999996, 80.7471, 128.00709999999992], [198.19799999999998, 120.08709999999996, 230.5368, 128.00709999999992], [320.5413, 120.08709999999996, 352.8234, 128.00709999999992], [431.82899999999995, 120.08709999999996, 455.2163999999999, 128.00709999999992]], [[51.5331, 131.59629999999993, 148.67189999999997, 139.5163], [198.19799999999998, 131.59629999999993, 230.5368, 139.51